Here is a board / steering-committee grade Risk Register with Mitigation Strategies, aligned to your AML / Compliance + RPA / IPA programme context.

⸻

Risk Register & Mitigation Plan

Risk Name	Risk Type	Description	Probability	Mitigation / Strategy
Incomplete or unclear requirements	Scope / Delivery	Compliance requirements may be high-level, inconsistent, or fragmented, leading to solution misfit and rework.	Medium	• Enforce structured requirement templates• Mandatory HLRD sign-off before vendor engagement• Conduct walkthrough workshops and playback sessions
Stakeholder availability constraints	Schedule / Resource	Compliance and operations teams may have limited time for workshops, validations, and testing.	Medium	• Pre-book governance calendar slots• Nominate BU focal owners• Escalation path via Compliance leadership
Late or contested requirement sign-off	Governance	Delays or disputes in requirement validation can stall downstream vendor and POC phases.	Medium	• Introduce formal stage-gate sign-offs• Time-boxed review cycles• Signed assumption and exclusion log
Overstated vendor capabilities	Vendor / Technical	Vendors may overstate functional or AI maturity, exposing gaps only during POC.	Medium	• Scenario-based demos only• Evidence-driven scoring framework• POC exit criteria tied to operational KPIs
Weak market coverage	Vendor / Strategic	Shortlisting may miss stronger or more suitable AML/IPA vendors.	Low	• Leverage peer bank references• Industry analyst input• Parallel discovery streams
NDA and legal delays	Legal / Schedule	Contractual or compliance checks may delay sensitive information sharing.	Low	• Pre-approved NDA templates• Parallel legal review• Early legal engagement
Budget constraints discovered late	Financial	Budget limits may restrict POC or implementation scope after vendor selection.	Medium	• Budget framing before RFP• Tiered solution options• Modular implementation approach
Dual board approval dependency	Governance	Projects exceeding RM300k require multiple boards, extending decision cycles.	High	• Align milestone calendar to board cycles• Pre-reads and executive briefings• Conditional approval models
Procurement cycle slippage	Procurement	Formal tender and evaluation processes may exceed planned durations.	High	• Procurement engaged at planning stage• Pre-aligned evaluation criteria• Parallel technical and commercial reviews
Contract negotiation delays	Legal / Commercial	Legal and commercial negotiations may delay Notice to Proceed.	Medium	• Commercial red-line boundaries pre-defined• Parallel technical mobilisation• Escalation committee
POC scope creep	Delivery	Poorly bounded POC may expand beyond validation objectives.	Medium	• Formal POC charter and KPI gates• Change control enforced• Weekly steering checkpoints
POC fails to demonstrate value	Delivery / Technical	Data quality, integration, or tooling constraints prevent POC success.	Medium	• Data readiness assessment before POC• Vendor technical deep-dives• Backup vendor strategy
Additional POC cycle required	Schedule / Cost	Initial POC inconclusive, requiring extension or second vendor.	Medium	• Design POC to answer “go/no-go” questions only• Multi-vendor shortlisting buffer• Fixed-duration POC window
Data access and quality issues	Technical / Operational	Compliance data may be incomplete, restricted, or unfit for testing.	Medium	• Early data profiling• Legal and risk clearance gates• Synthetic datasets prepared
Integration complexity underestimated	Technical	Dependencies with core systems may be more complex than expected.	Medium	• Architecture due diligence phase• Proof-of-connectivity tests• Dedicated GDTT integration sprint
User rejection risk	Adoption / Change	End-users may resist adoption or reject delivered workflows.	Medium	• Early user journey validation• Shadow operations and parallel run• Embedded change champions
Parallel run operational exposure	Operational Risk	Live shadow processing may create confusion or regulatory exposure.	Low	• Strict parallel run SOPs• Segregated environments• Compliance oversight during run
Regulatory misalignment	Compliance	Solution outputs may not meet audit, traceability, or regulator expectations.	Low	• Compliance embedded in design reviews• Audit-ready logging requirements• Regulator-aligned control mapping
Benefits not realised	Strategic / Financial	Automation may not translate into measurable productivity or risk gains.	Medium	• Benefits baseline before start• KPI ownership assigned• Benefits tracking built into governance


